<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Macronix lowers profit target.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Macronix lowers profit target.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan semiconductor maker Macronix International Co said on Wednesday it has lowered its 1996 pre-tax profit target to T$3.4 billion from the original forecast of T$4.2 billion.</p>
<p>The company also reduced its full-year sales target to T$10.7 billion from T$13.5 billion, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The firm attributed the lower-than-expected earning figures to sharp falls in international chip prices due to oversupply.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
